From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliv3rmoon <165517657+Oliv3rmoon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:50:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Eden: build eden-nx2 50fa86bbbc (Eden master with Switch 2
 support); the patches and derivations follow it

The eleven patches rebase onto it (one include conflict). Derivations follow eden-nx2's
code where it changed; two are dropped because upstream now does the same: the small-vector
include (upstream removed FixSmallVectorADL) and GetPseudoDeviceId without control data.
Solid NCZ games and updates are still read: Eden's new block reader stays behind ours.
The split GPU thread is stopped with the PS5 worker, reset between sessions, and an exception
on it ends the session like one on the worker.

(Cherry-picked from Oliv3rmoon/Nightshade 63e4561 for PS5-ECAM: Nightshade's own Eden patches 05 to
11, its checks and its port log are left out; the guest core's idle wait keeps this fork's
spin-then-sleep on eden-nx2's atomic flag, and Nightshade's interrupt timing, scheduler retry,
unmapped access log and NSZ reading, which this fork does not have, stay out.)
